COMPARED. Other AIs compared the answers sentence by sentence: each DIFFER entry is a place where the AIs said things that cannot both be true, each CHECK entry a sentence the comparison was not sure about (why: unsure = the judge was not sure, crossDirection = the two directions disagreed, noEvidence = no sentence was cited, numberMismatch = the numbers may not fit, numbersAbsent = the other answer has other numbers).
TASK. Write in the language of the QUESTION, in Markdown, and answer the QUESTION directly. Say what the answers agree on once. For every DIFFER entry, and every other place where the answers clearly differ, write that the AIs differ, name the AIs of each side exactly as written in "ais" and what each side says, and do not decide which side is right; when an answer gives its own reason or source for its side, you may add it. Mention CHECK entries with care. Mark what only one AI says with that AI's name, such as "(Codex only)" in English or "(Codex만)" in Korean. Add nothing that no answer says. Keep it shorter than the longest ANSWER.
